  <bioghist id="fa04f0ddedeb1c066be6c4aec1f206d5">
    <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
<p>Alta Starr is a somatic coach, bodyworker, and poet who worked for several years at the Ford Foundation. Starr joined the Ford Foundation in 2006 as a Program Officer in the Peace and Social Justice Program (PSJ) Governance and Civil Society unit (GCS). After a change in the Foundation's program structure, she became part of the Democracy, Rights, and Justice Program.
 
Starr started working as a trainer for Black Organizing for Leadership and Dignity (BOLD) at the project's inception. BOLD provides training and mentorship to Black organizers of social justice organizations. Starr previously worked as a teacher and a producer for news and music.</p>  </bioghist>
